<body>
    <h1>FIPS 140-3 Engineering Milestone Tracker</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p local-id=3D"4b7be4fd5c78">Go<img height=3D"250" style=3D"margin:=
 2px; border: 1px solid #ddd; box-sizing: border-box; vertical-align: text-=
bottom;" src=3D"f8b12c98c49c5238594e5842ffd01286bb044899b60ad25a5f5a1d64787=
4e96f" width=3D"250"> FIPS 140-3 is the US government standard for cryptogr=
aphic modules. CMVP is the Cryptographic Module Validation Program. CMVP te=
sts modules against the standard. CMVP issues the certificate. FedRAMP High=
 requires every service that touches federal data to run on a validated mod=
ule. Do not assume a module is validated. Prove it. Give the certificate nu=
mber and the evidence.</p>
<p local-id=3D"597adbed2588"><strong>Canonical guidance:</strong> Use the <=
a href=3D"https://cisco-sbg.atlassian.net/wiki/x/JB1jVQ" rel=3D"nofollow">F=
edRAMP High FIPS 140-3 Checklist for Engineering Teams</a> (page 1432558884=
) as the source of truth. This page tracks status against the 6-step workfl=
ow below. This page links to the Confluence section instead of repeating it=
.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6b205723bafa"><strong>Required statement when you report sta=
tus:</strong> Say <em>"This service uses CMVP-validated FIPS 140-3 cryptogr=
aphic modules in an approved manner."</em> Do not say <em>"FIPS certified."=
</em> Only modules get certified. See Confluence's <a href=3D"https://cisco=
-sbg.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CSCFGFAI/pages/1432558884/FedRAMP+High+FIPS+=
140-3+Checklist+for+Engineering+Teams+on+Cryptographic+Use+and+Documentatio=
n" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1432558884" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1=
3" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Common documentation mistakes to avoi=
d</a> for the full list of phrases to avoid.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1a1c931016b2"></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"c0adc29fce11" id=3D"FIPS140-3EngineeringMilestoneTracker-FI=
PS140-3=E2=80=94engineeringmilestones(IL2)">FIPS 140-3=E2=80=94 engineering=
 milestones (IL2)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"cf49e6b07887"><em><span style=3D"color: rgb(255,255,255);">=
=EE=84=93</span></em></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"6e=
871fdd-e48d-40bb-b269-a0d1c094b9b3" class=3D"confluenceTable">
