</div>
<hr local-id=3D"86ae7f9c460d" data-layout=3D"wide" data-width=3D"760">
<h2 local-id=3D"108617a3cbb9" id=3D"FIPS140-3EngineeringMilestoneTracker-Th=
e6-StepWorkflow">The 6-Step Workflow</h2>
<p local-id=3D"fd151c4e5877">Apply this sequence to every service. Apply th=
e steps in order. Do not skip a step.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c396280563e8"><strong>Step 1 =E2=80=94 List Components.</str=
ong> List every component. List every data flow. List every place your serv=
ice uses cryptography. See <a href=3D"https://cisco-sbg.atlassian.net/wiki/=
spaces/CSCFGFAI/pages/1432558884/FedRAMP+High+FIPS+140-3+Checklist+for+Engi=
neering+Teams+on+Cryptographic+Use+and+Documentation" data-linked-resource-=
id=3D"1432558884" data-linked-resource-version=3D"13" data-linked-resource-=
type=3D"page">What counts as in scope</a> for the full list of what you mus=
t inventory.</p>
<p local-id=3D"26c6fc15aade"><strong>Step 2 =E2=80=94 Generate CBOM.</stron=
g> Record the module name, vendor, version, and purpose for each component.=
 Confluence's <a href=3D"https://cisco-sbg.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CSCFGF=
AI/pages/1432558884/FedRAMP+High+FIPS+140-3+Checklist+for+Engineering+Teams=
+on+Cryptographic+Use+and+Documentation" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1432558=
884" data-linked-resource-version=3D"13" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page"=
>Verifying cryptographic usage with CBOM (FedRAMP Toolkit)</a> explains the=
 <code>fpa scan container</code> command and how to read its output. Reques=
t access to the <a href=3D"https://github.com/cisco-sbg-emu/FedRAMP-Toolkit=
" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">FedRAMP Toolkit repo</a> from <s=
trong>Sam Aydlette</strong> before you run a scan. See the <a href=3D"https=
://cisco-sbg.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CSCFGFAI/pages/1341269289/FedRAMP+To=
olkit" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1341269289" data-linked-resource-version=
=3D"27" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">FedRAMP Toolkit</a> page for wha=
t the toolkit covers.<br><br>
skills Developed by Abhijit: <a href=3D"https://github.com/cisco-sbg/clouds=
ec-FedRAMP-FIPS-140-3-skills" local-id=3D"ed49e692ace8" data-card-appearanc=
e=3D"inline" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://github.com/ci=
sco-sbg/cloudsec-FedRAMP-FIPS-140-3-skills</a> <br>
Generic CBOM toolkit: <a href=3D"https://github.com/cbomkit/cbomkit-theia" =
local-id=3D"491b470749f4" data-card-appearance=3D"inline" class=3D"external=
-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://github.com/cbomkit/cbomkit-theia</a></p>
<p class=3D"media-group"><img height=3D"250" style=3D"margin: 2px; border: =
1px solid #ddd; box-sizing: border-box; vertical-align: text-bottom;" src=
=3D"406032badeb5a8548990a6152887119e6c43a19d5aaabe451d4ac82e305958fc" width=
=3D"250"></p>
<p local-id=3D"1d978cf53011"><strong>Step 3 =E2=80=94 CMVP Mapping.</strong=
> Map each module to its certificate number. Confluence does not cover this=
 step in depth. Use the <a href=3D"#cmvp-certificate-lookup">CMVP Lookup</a=
> section below instead.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b6ee3beaaa10"><strong>Step 4 =E2=80=94 Verify FIPS Mode.</st=
rong> Confirm the config and flags enable FIPS mode. Confirm the self-tests=
 pass. Confirm the setting survives a restart. Confluence's <a href=3D"http=
s://cisco-sbg.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CSCFGFAI/pages/1432558884/FedRAMP+H=
igh+FIPS+140-3+Checklist+for+Engineering+Teams+on+Cryptographic+Use+and+Doc=
umentation" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1432558884" data-linked-resource-ver=
sion=3D"13" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Programming language guidanc=
e</a> gives the exact commands for each runtime: Go, Java, Python, Node.js,=
 Rust, and C/C++. <a href=3D"https://cisco-sbg.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CS=
CFGFAI/pages/1432558884/FedRAMP+High+FIPS+140-3+Checklist+for+Engineering+T=
eams+on+Cryptographic+Use+and+Documentation" data-linked-resource-id=3D"143=
2558884" data-linked-resource-version=3D"13" data-linked-resource-type=3D"p=
age">Common crypto paths beyond OpenSSL that engineering teams must verify<=
/a> lists the runtime and library risks, including Guacamole, Nginx, Postgr=
es, and librdkafka. See <a href=3D"https://cisco-sbg.atlassian.net/wiki/spa=
ces/CSCFGFAI/pages/1432558884/FedRAMP+High+FIPS+140-3+Checklist+for+Enginee=
ring+Teams+on+Cryptographic+Use+and+Documentation" data-linked-resource-id=
=3D"1432558884" data-linked-resource-version=3D"13" data-linked-resource-ty=
pe=3D"page">What Cloud9 manages vs. what engineering teams must do</a> for =
the split between what Cloud9 handles at the OS layer and what your team ow=
ns.</p>
<p local-id=3D"54d2e2814b48"><strong>Step 5 =E2=80=94 Runtime Validation.</=
strong> Run live connection tests. Run negative tests to confirm the servic=
e rejects disallowed crypto. Confluence's <a href=3D"https://cisco-sbg.atla=
ssian.net/wiki/spaces/CSCFGFAI/pages/1432558884/FedRAMP+High+FIPS+140-3+Che=
cklist+for+Engineering+Teams+on+Cryptographic+Use+and+Documentation" data-l=
inked-resource-id=3D"1432558884" data-linked-resource-version=3D"13" data-l=
inked-resource-type=3D"page">Platform and component guidance</a> gives plat=
form-specific checklists for ALB, EKS, remote access, and managed security =
components.</p>
<p local-id=3D"062629d89294"><strong>Step 6 =E2=80=94 Compliance Assessment=
.</strong> Write one report. Cover scope, evidence, findings, gaps, and con=
clusion. See <a href=3D"https://cisco-sbg.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CSCFGFA=
I/pages/1432558884/FedRAMP+High+FIPS+140-3+Checklist+for+Engineering+Teams+=
on+Cryptographic+Use+and+Documentation" data-linked-resource-id=3D"14325588=
84" data-linked-resource-version=3D"13" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">=
What good looks like</a> for what a good report contains.</p>
<p local-id=3D"78bb0e87f0e8">FIPS 140-2 certificates are aging out. Conflue=
nce's <a href=3D"https://cisco-sbg.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CSCFGFAI/pages=
/1432558884/FedRAMP+High+FIPS+140-3+Checklist+for+Engineering+Teams+on+Cryp=
tographic+Use+and+Documentation" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1432558884" dat=
a-linked-resource-version=3D"13" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">FIPS 14=
0-3 transition timeline</a> explains what this means for the OpenSSL provid=
er in your image. This page keeps the certificate numbers current in the ta=
ble below, since Confluence does not track that data live.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"3057c402699d" data-layout=3D"wide" data-width=3D"760">
<h2 local-id=3D"eaf52a351a5f" id=3D"FIPS140-3EngineeringMilestoneTracker-CM=
VPCertificateLookup">CMVP Certificate Lookup</h2>
<p local-id=3D"96b452c898f3">Step 3 is the hardest step to automate. CMVP h=
as no bulk export. CMVP has no API. CMVP has only a <a href=3D"https://csrc=
.nist.gov/projects/cryptographic-module-validation-program/validated-module=
s/search" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">search form</a>. Every l=
ookup is manual.</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"142a030bef0c">
<li local-id=3D"061a42d2d02b">
<p local-id=3D"94fbed7847e7">Pull the module name, version, and vendor from=
 your CBOM.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b8be254a907a">
<p local-id=3D"b70c56e49441">Search CMVP by <strong>vendor</strong> name. V=
endor name matches more reliably than module name. Set status to Active fir=
st.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a4c85b007faa">
<p local-id=3D"62cae3b33f4e">Shortlist certificates with a similar module n=
ame.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b7a76803b849">
<p local-id=3D"390936bd4b02">Open the candidate certificate. Confirm the ex=
act version, operational environment, and caveats match your deployment.</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"33e3d7cfa1fc">
<p local-id=3D"e62a5abaeb8d">If you find a match, record the certificate nu=
mber in your tracker row. If you find no match, write <strong>"unmatched =
=E2=80=94 needs manual verification."</strong> Never guess.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a252d6748cc7">
<p local-id=3D"9a923c16e9c1">Add any newly confirmed certificate to the tab=
le below.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1800" data-layout=3D"full-width" data-local-id=
=3D"c2ba47937efd" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
