<p local-id=3D"562bf17806b5"></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"ff28e5db6f67" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"f85d2068c01f">CSC (and SWG)&nbsp; currently uses FIPS provid=
er package 3.0.<a href=3D"https://9.8.0.30" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"=
nofollow">9.8.0.30</a>.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0ad3253b6d3a"><a href=3D"https://cisco-sbg.atlassian.net/wik=
i/spaces/dev/pages/1486553099/Windows+CiscoSSL+8.5+FIPS+3.0.9+Hybrid+Setup+=
Guide" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1486553099" data-linked-resource-version=
=3D"7" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Windows CiscoSSL 8.5 + FIPS 3.0.9=
 Hybrid Setup Guide</a> maps 8.0.30 provider to CMVP certificate #5430.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e282a9268384">And according to <a href=3D"https://csrc.nist.=
gov/projects/cryptographic-module-validation-program/certificate/5430" clas=
s=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">NIST</a>, 5430 has active FIPS 140-3 L=
evel 1 validation through November 17, 2029.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c686ebea35ea">However, a bug has been identified where FIPS =
mode is not enabled due to a path change introduced during OpenSSL8 change =
last November. Exception request has been raised to get this into MR20 buil=
d targeted for release by Mid Sep.</p></td>
</tr>
